invariant: INV-73
file: src/tcp_nonblocking.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: a client keeps cfg.buf when it connects, so its handshake plaintext,
  the server's certificates among it, stays in a buffer the caller gives
  to the next handshake, and the session still names the buffer.

--- old
            r->t.state = CH_ST_CONNECTED;
            tlsi_give_back_buf(&r->t);
--- new
            r->t.state = CH_ST_CONNECTED;
